/**
 * Harikathāmṛtasāra of Śrī Jagannātha Dāsa (Kannada, bhāminī ṣaṭpadi): sandhis 3–10.
 * One Mantra per sandhi, in Kannada script (sourceScript: 'kannada'). Sandhis 1 and 2 are in harikathamrutasara.ts.
 *
 * Sandhi order is that of the Bemmatti Venkaṭēśācār mūla edition and kn.wikisource
 * (19 Karmavimocana, 20 Guṇatāratamya, 21 Bṛhattāratamya, 22 Sakaladuritanivāraṇa,
 * 23 Kalpasādhana, 24 Bimbāparokṣa). Some online copies list 19–24 in another order.
 * The closing Phalastuti (a 33rd sandhi in some copies) is not by Jagannātha Dāsa and is not included.
 *
 * Method (Nov 2026). Every verse was built from several independent copies and collated
 * akṣara by akṣara (a script aligned each copy to a base text, listed every place where
 * the copies differ, and chose the reading backed by most copies):
 *  - HK: harshalarajesh Google Site 'Harikathamruthasara' (SGP Char), a Latin-transliterated
 *    six-line text with word glosses, chapter pages 3-32.
 *  - WS: kn.wikisource.org, ಹರಿಕಥಾಮೃತಸಾರ/<sandhi> (typed; sandhis 3-13 in printed form, 14-32 word-separated).
 *  - RAO: raocollectionssongs.blogspot.com, pages 03-32 (word-separated Kannada text; Rao and
 *    kn.wikisource agree closely for sandhis 14-32, so for those they count as one copy).
 *  - BEM: the Bemmatti Venkaṭēśācār mūla edition (archive.org harikathamrutasara-mula-bemmatti-venkateshachar),
 *    machine-read; Y25: the 1925 edition (archive.org HarikathaamrutaSaaravu_-_JagannathDaasaru);
 *    D30: the 1930 DLI edition (in.ernet.dli.2015.362896). These three scans are OCR and carry
 *    aspirate / vowel-length / ಳ-ಲ misreadings, so a scan reading counts less than a typed one.
 * Where the copies split evenly the Bemmatti reading was followed if another copy agreed with it;
 * otherwise the reading was chosen by sense and metre (the verse numbers are in each contentNote).
 * Word division and the six lines follow the printed text (mātrā 14/14/22 · 14/14/22; some lines
 * count 13, 15, 21 or 23 because of conjuncts across line ends, as in sandhis 1-2).
 * Corrections made on the way: systematic ಛ for ಚ and ತ್ರು for ತೃ in the typed copies; WS numbering
 * slips in sandhis 8 and 17; sandhi 12 (45 verses) and 22 (35 verses) are longer than WS/Bemmatti-draft counts
 * because those copies omit verses that HK, Rao or the 1925 print have (12.26-45; 22.29, 22.34).
 * Printed-edition check (Nov 2026, sandhis 3-10). Every verse was then read against page images of
 *  - BEM: Harikathamrutasara mula, ed. Bemmatti Venkatesacharya ('Sukhabodhasagara'), archive.org
 *    harikathamrutasara-mula-bemmatti-venkateshachar (leaves n51-n186; the leaf with 6.10-13 is missing);
 *  - SW: Harikathamritasara with the Kannada vyakhyana of Sri Sankarshana Odeyar, vols 1-2, archive.org
 *    harikathamrita-saara-1-sri-jannatha-dasaru-sri-sankarshana-wodeyar and ...-saara-2-...;
 *  - BP: Harikathamrutasara with the Bhavaprakashike of Sri Padmanabha Dasa, vol 1, archive.org
 *    HarikathamrutasaraWithBhavaprakashikeCommentary_-_1_-_JagannathadasaruPadmanabhaDasaru (= DLI 2015.363030);
 *  and the typed madhwafestivals.com sandhi pages (word-separated) as a further witness. Where BEM and the
 *  commentaries differ, the reading that keeps the metre and has two printed witnesses was chosen; the
 *  counts in the meanings follow the SW commentary and the BEM verse headings.
 */

